OL,3,AZambia courts sealed off as election
OL,4,Apetition deadline looms
OL,5,
OL,6,FCourt premises in the Zambian capital,
OL,7,FLusaka, and elsewhere have been shut as
OL,8,Fthe deadline for filing a petition
OL,9,Fagainst the outcome of the recent
OL,10,Fpresidential election approaches.
OL,12,FAn unusual police presence has been
OL,13,Freported at some courts, which have
OL,14,Fbeen taped off to prevent access.
OL,16,FOpposition candidate Brian Mundubile
OL,17,Fsaid he would challenge the election
OL,18,Fresult, citing irregularities, after
OL,19,Fcoming second with a 38% share of the
OL,20,Fvote. Incumbent Hakainde Hichilema won
OL,21,Fa second term with 60%.
OL,23,APub: 24-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
